    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I'll read the original test and CUT source to understand what needs to be improved.Now I understand the test. The `testResolveVariable` test verifies that `resolveVariable` is called with correct arguments during substitution. The original class has dead code: `doTestNoReplace`, `doTestReplace`, and the `values` field/setUp/tearDown are never used by this single test. I'll clean those up and clarify the magic position numbers.The improved test compiled successfully. The refactored file removes all dead code (unused helper methods, `values` field, and lifecycle methods) and replaces the magic position numbers 3 and 10 with named constants accompanied by a Javadoc comment that maps each index to its character position in `\"Hi ${name}!\"`."
